---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = "+16072289269";
const phoneDisplay = "+1 (607) 228-9269";
---
<Layout title="AC Leaking Water Gastonia NC | Condensate Drain Clog | acrepairgastonianc.com" description="Water pooling around your AC in Gastonia? Blocked condensate drain or frozen coil. Prevent mold and damage. Call +1 (607) 228-9269.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/problems/">Problems</a> / Leaking Water</p>
      <h1>AC Leaking Water in Gastonia</h1>
      <p>Water pooling around your unit signals a blocked condensate drain or frozen coil melting. Unchecked, this causes mold and ceiling damage.</p>
      <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-white btn-lg">Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-block">
      <p><span class="badge badge-danger">Urgent — Act Now</span></p>
      <p>Most AC water leaks at the indoor unit are condensate drainage problems. Algae, sludge, and debris clog the drain line; the pan overflows or the float switch shuts the system down. In Gastonia humidity, mold can establish within 24–48 hours.</p>
      <p>Professional drain line cleaning clears the full path and confirms free flow. If ice was present, underlying airflow or refrigerant issues must also be fixed. See <a href="/services/drain-line-cleaning/">Drain Line Cleaning</a> and <a href="/services/emergency-ac-repair/">Emergency AC Repair</a>.</p>
      <div class="cta-box">
        <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
